    "tag_name": "v1.3.0",
    "name": "Morphlet v1.3.0",
    "body": "# Morphlet v1.3.0\n\n## Select files, then tap one key\n\n- On macOS, select files in Finder and press and release Cmd on its own.\n- On Windows, select files in an active File Explorer window and press and release Ctrl on its own.\n- Change the modifier or disable this gesture in Studio \u2192 Settings.\n- Other key combinations and modifier-click selection are excluded from the gesture.\n- Fix installed Windows selection/drag helper packaging by shipping the PowerShell script outside app.asar.\n- Keep Option/Alt-drag as a separate drag gesture.\n\n## GNOME Files integration\n\nIn the installed Linux app, open Studio Settings and choose Install GNOME Files action. Select files in Nautilus, right-click, then Scripts \u2192 Morphlet to open the selected local files directly in the wheel. Requires Python 3. GNOME Wayland restricts global modifier-only capture, so Ctrl-only is not promised there; use the Files action or Studio drag/drop.\n\n## Validation and distribution\n\n51 automated tests pass locally, and the implementation passes macOS Apple Silicon, macOS Intel, Windows x64 and Linux x64 package builds. Windows CI checks the installed helper; trusted macOS builds verify app signatures and DMG contents. Interactive desktop gesture testing is still needed across system configurations.\n\nmacOS packages remain ad-hoc signed without Apple notarization. Windows installers remain unsigned.\n",
